{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts","id":1063786,"title":"Mage Boons/Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-17T03:24:12-07:00","id":1063786,"title":"Mage Boons/Gifts","content":"Lets assume that a Vampire actually saves the life of a Mage for certain death. Then the Mage offers the Vampire a Boon / Gift in return. What would a Vampire would ask from a Mage in return? What would be an ideal gift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T03:38:53-07:00","id":1063790,"title":"","content":"Depends on the mage. I believe having Mental Shield with indefinite duration would be a godsend considering Dominate, Majesty and Nightmare, but that's a lot since it costs a Willpower dot for the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T03:56:01-07:00","id":1063794,"title":"","content":"IMMUNITY TO FIRE!<br /> <br /> Ahem, yes. So, would depend on the path or available arcana of the Mage in question. (also on how good a boon you want it to be) <br /> <br /> Fate - Luck (Exceptional Luck for a specific encounter, Red/Green Light for a year)<br /> Time - Depending on power level of Mage, possibly even shunting back to before vampirisation, or to a more recent choice to be undone, or a divination<br /> Death - Healing? Ability to interact with ghosts for a while? Assistance of ghosts for a thing.<br /> Matter - cool overloaded magical gear?<br /> Prime - cool overloaded magical gear?<br /> Forces - IMMUNITY TO FIRE! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> Spirit - Ability to interact with spirits for a while? Assistance of spirits for a thing. <br /> Life - Um. Well. Heal their puppy? <br /> Mind - Provide immunity to mind-affecting effects? Buff a mental stat for a while.<br /> Space - Teleport somewhere. Provide a safe space?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11842-aeryes","name":"Aeryes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11842_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:06:02-07:00","id":1063800,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the spell can't be active for more than one week without starting to deteriorate unless it's constantly updated (which sounds more like a service rather than a one time boon) or basically cost an XP for the mage to keep it going longer.<br /> But during that week you might even be immune to sunlight. (Doesn't help against Lethargic unlesd the mage has the right Arcana for dealing with that as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:09:50-07:00","id":1063803,"title":"","content":"I think a Mage can spare 1 XP for a Indefinite Spell if they really want to say &quot;thank you&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:09:53-07:00","id":1063804,"title":"","content":"Nothing. The vampire is smart enough to know that carrying around shards of Awakened magic can be used against him in a way that vamipre society isn't prepared to deal with. Awakend magic is a double edged sword","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:15:04-07:00","id":1063805,"title":"","content":"Howso, and why would the vampire have access to that kind of information?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T04:19:18-07:00","id":1063806,"title":"","content":"If the vampire actually trusts the mage I'd go with immunity to fire/sunlight(the second is a strong maybe possible) or perhaps a pocket world that he has access to that is keyed to only him.<br /> Sure it would be nice to be able to have ghouls wake you up or what not, but it's also nice to be certain that outside of other magic to invade, you don't have to worry about anyone coming to stake you at your weakest. The safehouse burns down, is raided or blown up? None of it bothers the pocket dimension. Just exit when the fire is gone and rebuild. Should get a lot of use out of it until it's compromised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11759,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","user":"Bonreu","date":". 03-17-2017, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T05:03:37-07:00","id":1063812,"title":"","content":"The problem with the pocket dimension gift is that that assumes you saved the life of a master of Space. Obviously not impossible but, just by sheer probability, not likely. Most mages have a maximum skill of being a disciple in one or two arcana. A decent number make it to adept, but that still doesn't get you a pocket dimension.<br /> <br /> More realistically would be the request to become immune to fire. Most mages probably know at least one other mage that could cast such a spell if they weren't capable of doing it themselves. And if transferring your life debt to another mage is too onerous to him, then you can probably come up with something.<br /> <br /> In fact, here's a quick list of useful spells mages could cast on a vampire. This list is based on the presumption that the mage is a disciple in the appropriate arcanum.<br /> <br /> Death: Without a Trace, Soul Armor, Ghost Gate, Ghost shield<br /> Fate: Monkey's Paw, Warding Gesture<br /> Forces: FIRE SHIELD! Mwahahahaha!<br /> Life: Web of Life<br /> Matter: Alchemist's Touch, Aegis<br /> Mind: One Mind Two Thoughts, Mental Shield, Augment Mind, Universal Language<br /> Prime: Pierce Deception, Wards and Signs, Ephemeral Enchantment<br /> Space: Ground Eater, The Outward and Inward Eye, Veil Sympathy, Ward, <br /> Spirit: Exorcist's Eye, Ephemeral Shield, Gossamer Touch, Shadow Walk<br /> Time: Constant Presence, Shield of Chronos, Acceleration<br /> <br /> Technically a few of those spells aren't spells you'd cast on the vampire itself, but they'd still be useful. I didn't include co-location because of the need to reach, like, 5 or 6 times to have a visible, indefinite, keyed portal. That goes a bit further than just spending a willpower dot and dips well into a decent amount of mana usage. It's a life debt, but mages are still crafty and stingy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 03-17-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T05:30:34-07:00","id":1063814,"title":"","content":"I would say that it depends on if the Vampire was the PC, the Mage was the PC or if both were the PC, As a ST you want to try and keep a hold of the reigns on really fantastic spells that are in favor of the PC because you do not want to upset the balance of your campaign. If it is an NPC that is receiving the Boon go hog wild and then let them be integral to the story as either a menace or an occasional powerful resource.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T05:40:49-07:00","id":1063818,"title":"","content":"... A Vampire who saves the life of an Adept of Time could perhaps not unreasonably ask for them to save them from their condition with a persistent Rewrite History spell to retcon their Vampirism.<br /> <br /> In terms of other, less world-shaking favors... Well if an indefinite spell is too much to ask for, then the Mage might be willing to perform a few short-term boons in keeping with their skillset.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T07:09:08-07:00","id":1063835,"title":"","content":"If I were a vampire who saved a Mage, I'd offer them a little of my vitae - to help them get on their feet, you know? Then I'd wait to see what the Mage decides to offer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T07:13:35-07:00","id":1063836,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if the mage has a bit of Life and is brave (read foolish) enough, the mage could let the vampire use him as a miniature blood bank for a little while. He could heal the damage done and remove any condition stemming from blood loss, and the Kiss feels pleasurable enough so why not?<br /> <br /> <br /> Ninja'd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T09:52:21-07:00","id":1063912,"title":"","content":"Who is the PC in this scenario and what does the Mage have to work with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T13:23:32-07:00","id":1064006,"title":"","content":"The PC is actually the leader of a Carthian Covenant and they saved a Death/Matter Mage from some Hunters. So in return the Mage offered the leader a gift or boon for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11988-montgomery-crobes","name":"Montgomery Crobes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T13:50:09-07:00","id":1064017,"title":"","content":"Generally, a Carthian would love some way to strengthen their cause. Getting rid of the Invictus would help greatly. Some ghost minions and spies, possibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T15:59:28-07:00","id":1064066,"title":"","content":"Spy on an enemy, kill an enemy, or cover up for the vampire depending on what the mage can do.<br /> <br /> Reasons:<br /> 1. always best to keep it simple when cashing in a favor<br /> 2. not asking for much encourages secrecy which should be part of the favor, always<br /> 3. nice way to assert superiority and let a mage know how little their life is worth to vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 03-17-2017, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-17T17:34:15-07:00","id":1064093,"title":"","content":"While a vampire saving the life of an archmaster is unlikely, Fangs might find an opportunity to save someone Wandsy cares about. This only increases in probability the weaker Wandsy is.<br /> <br /> Information, whether on a supernatural problem or spying on a foe or other thing, is an excellent use of a mage ally. Fixing hunger or Ignoring the sun would be more obvious things to <i>request</i>...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T01:03:17-07:00","id":1064213,"title":"","content":"I think the Vampire would say you owe me, then stuff that favor up his sleeve as an extra Ace for the day he really needs it. Preferably a day when his own unlife hangs in the balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T02:11:43-07:00","id":1064224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1063800#post1063800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the spell can't be active for more than one week without starting to deteriorate unless it's constantly updated (which sounds more like a service rather than a one time boon) or basically cost an XP for the mage to keep it going longer.<br /> But during that week you might even be immune to sunlight. (Doesn't help against Lethargic unlesd the mage has the right Arcana for dealing with that as well.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, can mage just not use Advanced Duration, get some Duration Factory by takeing few -2 and ending with spell cast on vampire for whole years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T03:18:42-07:00","id":1064238,"title":"","content":"Unless the mage keeps the spell under their spell control (which nobody would for a whole year) the spell would start mutating. That's why it's called unsafe relinquishing and frowned upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-18T20:31:59-07:00","id":1064632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1064213#post1064213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Vampire would say you owe me, then stuff that favor up his sleeve as an extra Ace for the day he really needs it. Preferably a day when his own unlife hangs in the balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly how <i>I'd</i> play it, provided I knew enough about mage society not to need such data on a more immediate basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T04:40:53-07:00","id":1064705,"title":"","content":"Well lest not forget Sleepwalkers can hold spells for mages, and last I checked other supernatural are sleepwalkers. So the Mage could hand the spell over to the Vampire as he does sympathetic tie to a mage. Allowing the mage to grant a spell boon without spending exp, losing control, or using up his own spell control limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T04:43:40-07:00","id":1064707,"title":"","content":"Vampires are their own template not sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T05:32:23-07:00","id":1064714,"title":"","content":"To clarify: Sleepwalkers are humans with both Integrity and any kind of Supernatural Merit or other kind of supernatural power. That means there's several templates (ghouls, wolf-blooded, proximi, all the Merit templates from Hurt Locker) that are always Sleepwalkers, but vampires are not one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T05:52:17-07:00","id":1064720,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the opening section on flag bearers say that technically anyone can hold spells for you, just having a sleeper do it is a idiotic move?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T06:08:37-07:00","id":1064723,"title":"","content":"&quot;The truth is, technically, anyone with a sympathetic tie to a mage can carry spells for her.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes. That's very much true. Vampires not being Sleepwalkers does not mean they can't carry spells. The book also goes on to mention that Dissonance is the reason doing it on a Sleeper won't work, and vampires do not cause Dissonance.<br /> However, you'd need to maintain at least medium sympathetic connection. That requires either a spell or that the vampire and the mage works very closely together. More than casual acquaintances. So basically unworkable unless they are actual friends who keep hanging out or the mage knows Space 3 and can bolster the weak sympathetic connection gained from being the subject of the mage's spell. Probably in the form of combi-casting so Web-Weaver won't take up a second slot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-19-2017, 09:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T06:14:40-07:00","id":1064724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1064723#post1064723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The truth is, technically, anyone with a sympathetic tie to a mage can carry spells for her.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes. That's very much true. Vampires not being Sleepwalkers does not mean they can't carry spells. The book also goes on to mention that Dissonance is the reason doing it on a Sleeper won't work, and vampires do not cause Dissonance.<br /> However, you'd need to maintain at least medium sympathetic connection. That requires either a spell or that the vampire and the mage works very closely together. More than casual acquaintances. So basically unworkable unless they are actual friends who keep hanging out or the mage knows Space 3 and can bolster the weak sympathetic connection gained from being the subject of the mage's spell. Probably in the form of combi-casting so Web-Weaver won't take up a second slot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. Only hiccup in this is when a mage lends a spell to another mage. What then? I can't wait to see the working FAQ thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T06:31:40-07:00","id":1064730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1064724#post1064724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I agree. Only hiccup in this is when a mage lends a spell to another mage. What then? I can't wait to see the working FAQ thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd go with each spell you hold for another mage counts vs your Max spells and can have up to the normal sympathy limit even if it pushes you above your limit. <br /> But the is my opinion and nothing more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T06:44:57-07:00","id":1064733,"title":"","content":"That would create some fun feudal dynamic where Masters use Apprentices to sustain their spells as a form of tuition. <br /> [In exchange, I guess a Master could sometimes allow usage of their Soul Stone by best apprentice.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T06:47:50-07:00","id":1064734,"title":"","content":"Yea, I would do that too but it would be great to hear some official position before house ruling it. There is <b>a lot</b> of questions that are surfacing every now and then - and its been almost a year since publishing of M:tA 2E. FAQ thread? Why bother with basic consumer service? Meh. Let them chase and search for developers answers across multiple forums. That will do.<br /> Edit: I feel better now.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> Hmm. That seems cool, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T09:26:24-07:00","id":1064787,"title":"","content":"In fairness, I believe the technical term for the amount Dave has on his plate right now is &quot;fuckton&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T09:48:48-07:00","id":1064796,"title":"","content":"So you are saying that Dave is the only person who can compile the FAQ? <br /> Don't get me wrong. I think that the 2E is a great game writen by a very talented people (so much more user friendly than 1E) but has a lot of grey areas that beg to be asnwered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T10:08:11-07:00","id":1064800,"title":"","content":"Well, as the developer Dave would be the most qualified to write the FAQ. But even if he redirected the job to someone else that person would have to get done with their backlog of work on all projects they're involved with.<br /> I'm also frustrated that the FAQ takes so much time, but I kinda get why. But I do wish it had higher priority so that the book that is already out will get it's errata soon after it came out. My understanding 