Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:42:31-07:00","id":1064964,"title":"","content":"So the Vampire is a carthian and the Mage is a Moros? have the moros use a death veiling spell on the vampires political enemies, what would the spell do you ask? reproduce the black veiny soul marks of Amarnath in its targets. as its a low level effect (2 dots) it could be cast on multiple targets and with significant duration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T15:59:58-07:00","id":1064979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1064937#post1064937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's because some 'grey areas' might be cleared up in Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some, yea. And waiting 2 years (from publishing Core to publishing SoS) for a FAQ is ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T16:56:56-07:00","id":1065013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1064796#post1064796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you are saying that Dave is the only person who can compile the FAQ?</div> </div> </div> </div>That might depend on if he's being paid or not. Dave also asked for requests for legacies to convert that we haven't seen yet, and he explicitly mentioned he wasn't going to be paid for it. I suspect an FAQ could be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T18:02:05-07:00","id":1065031,"title":"","content":"From what I understood the FAQ was going to be something done for free, as such I expect it will be on the very-most back burner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T11:50:53-07:00","id":1065339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1064723#post1064723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The truth is, technically, anyone with a sympathetic tie to a mage can carry spells for her.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes. That's very much true. Vampires not being Sleepwalkers does not mean they can't carry spells. The book also goes on to mention that Dissonance is the reason doing it on a Sleeper won't work, and vampires do not cause Dissonance.<br /> However, you'd need to maintain at least medium sympathetic connection. That requires either a spell or that the vampire and the mage works very closely together. More than casual acquaintances. So basically unworkable unless they are actual friends who keep hanging out or the mage knows Space 3 and can bolster the weak sympathetic connection gained from being the subject of the mage's spell. Probably in the form of combi-casting so Web-Weaver won't take up a second slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>We encountered this in a game I'm playing, and we went back and forth on whether the section intends &quot;anyone&quot; to mean &quot;any normal human, not just Sleepwalkers&quot; or the broader &quot;anyone at all, including other Supernaturals, as long as they are capable of consenting to holding the spell.&quot; I asked the question here before, and people seemed to think the section intends the first. We ended up going with that for the simple reason that I'm in a crossover game and allowing Supernatural creatures to hold spells greatly increases a Mage's power. Specifically one like mine, who is a Mind Adept. Familiar is a 4 dot Mind/Spirit/Death spell that creates perfect Sympathy. Travelling into your own Oneiros and making many of its denizens Familiars gives you spell batteries - they hold the one that makes them a Familiar, and they hold the other one that you want.<br /> <br /> It's a little more dangerous for Death/Spirit Familiars, but they are also more likely to find ephemeral beings willing to accept since the Familiar condition is more beneficial to them. Stick them in your Sanctum and they are protected from essence bleed, can defend your Sanctum, and can hold spells that make you and your Sanctum magically protected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:21:07-07:00","id":1065388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ifisa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1065339#post1065339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little more dangerous for Death/Spirit Familiars, but they are also more likely to find ephemeral beings willing to accept since the Familiar condition is more beneficial to them. Stick them in your Sanctum and they are protected from essence bleed, can defend your Sanctum, and can hold spells that make you and your Sanctum magically protected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost and Spirit familiars are protected from Essence bleed by the Familiar spell, you don't need to put them in your Sanctum for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T13:50:39-07:00","id":1065414,"title":"","content":"Sort of getting back to the original post, if the Mage is being played in character and the Vampire did just save your life (and you aren't a selfish ass) would you really (in character) hesitate to make the small sacrifice in experience to repay the favor (by giving a Will power dot)?<br /> \u200bAs ST I would personally try to encourage that on the part of the player by at the least rewarding it with a Beat. I would also tell the player that this would be the perfect in story explanation for taking a point in Contact Vampire or even a points in Allies.<br /> \u200bI might even give them the point in Contact for free as a story reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-20T16:58:06-07:00","id":1065498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1063786-mage-boons-gifts?p=1065388#post1065388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghost and Spirit familiars are protected from Essence bleed by the Familiar spell, you don't need to put them in your Sanctum for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I meant that they get the benefit of that - which is a huge boon you can use to bargain to have them as magical guard dogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}